Orchestration techniques:
---------------------------
-> Concurrent Orchestration:
	- When tasks can run at the same time, either all agents or some agents.
	- Title, Graphics, Content
	- Teamwork orchestration, multiple techniques.
	- Problem solving scenarios, voting
	- Parallel execution, Faster
	
	- Do not use this, when agents are dependent on each other.
	- Shared context.
	- Sequence of steps.
	- ConcurrentBuilder and get_outputs()
	
-> Sequential Orchestration:
	- One agent after the other in a sequence.
	- Series of steps in a specific order.
	- each agent relies on the previous agent for input.
	- each agent passes some info to the next agent.
	- When tasks cannot be run in parallel, must be sequential.
	- Each step is refinement. Time consuming.
	
	- Do not use this, when your agents can run in parallel without affecting the functionality.
	- A single agent can do everything.
	- If one agent makes a mistake, you cannot correct it.
	- SequentialBuilder and WorkflowOutputEvent 
	
-> Group chat orchestration:
	- Human in the loop facility
	- Each agent can be executed more than once.
	- Group chat manager decides who will speak when, which agent will execute when.
	- Collaboration, Discussion between agents.
	- Maker-checker loops -> One agent will do something and send for review to second agent. Second agent will send back comments to the first agent. First agent will implement the comments and send back for review.
	- Human oversight is possible / needed.
	- Conversation as a group between agents.
	
	- Do not use this when you have a simple task at hand, linear pipeline, sequential tasks.
	- GroupChatBuilder and get_outputs()
	
-> Handoff orchestration:
	- Specialized agents which can perform specific tasks, but you cannot determine the order of execution.
	- Need for calling an agent arises within the conversation.
	- Dynamic in nature, depending on situation, agent will be called.
	- one agent hands over control to another agent.
	- Human in the loop option.
	- Clearly define when an agent should pass control to another agent (which agent).
	
	- Do not use this when you have a Simple task, sequential.
	- Order is fixed. 
	- Do not use when routing logic is complex.
	- Routing is simple - If-else.

-> Magentic orchestration:
	- Dynamic and complex.
	- A big problem, whose solution or process is unknown.
	- Set of tasks -> Progress check -> If yes, continue. If no progress, then rework.
	- Complex or open-ended problem, no known or predetermined solution or approach.
	- Feedback from multiple agents continuously.
	- Human review at the end.
	- Step by step approach, dynamic approach. Can change in iterations if problem is not being solved.
	- Rely on multiple factors to take a decision.
	- Multiple iterations. Time consuming.
	
	- Do not use this when you have a simple task.
	- Do not need to divide the task into smaller tasks.
	- When you want speed.
	- MagenticBuilder and WorkflowOutputEvent
	
